Here are the two files:

**`SortableList.razor`** — the template with `@typeparam TItem`, a `<ul>` loop using `@key`, and Move Up/Down buttons (disabled at boundaries).

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — the `partial class` code-behind:

- Copies `Items` into a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet` (never mutates the original).
- Swaps elements on move, then invokes `OnOrderChanged` with a read-only copy of the reordered list.

**Usage** matches your example — just note the template parameter name is `ItemTemplate`:

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private List<TaskItem> tasks = [ /* ... */ ];

    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> reordered)
    {
        tasks = reordered.ToList();
    }
}
```
